Spec: SpecDD Validation Result

Platform: IntelliJ Platform / Kotlin

Purpose:
  Represent validation results and diagnostic issue messages.

Owns:
  ./SpecDDValidationResult.kt

Can modify:
  ./SpecDDValidationResult.kt

Can read:
  /src/test/kotlin/ai/specdd/idea/validation/SpecDDValidationResultBehaviorSpec.kt

Must:
  Store validation issues in `SpecDDValidationResult`.
  Treat an empty issue list as valid.
  Treat a nonempty issue list as invalid.
  Store each issue range, message, and optional suggestion.
  Use the raw message as the display message when no suggestion exists.
  Append `Did you mean '<label>'?` to display messages when a suggestion exists.
  Keep display messages deterministic.
  Cover valid results, invalid results, and display-message formatting in tests.

Must not:
  Compute validation rules.
  Create IntelliJ annotations.
  Define highlighting colors.
